const faqs = [
  {
    q: "How do projects start, and what's the payment structure?",
    a: 'Every project begins with a discovery call to define scope and fit. Once agreed, I send a fixed quote and a signed agreement. Payments are split — typically 50% before kickoff and 50% before launch, with larger projects broken into 40/30/30. No work starts until the first payment lands.',
  },
  {
    q: 'What does each project cost?',
    a: 'Pricing depends on scope, complexity, and timeline. Most projects start at $3,000 and scale from there. You receive a fixed quote after the discovery call — no hourly billing, no surprise invoices, no fees added mid-project.',
  },
  {
    q: 'How long does a typical project take?',
    a: 'Most projects run between 3 and 8 weeks, depending on scope. The exact timeline is fixed in the agreement before kickoff and tracked stage by stage in your project workspace.',
  },
  {
    q: "How do projects start, and what's the payment structure?",
    a: 'Every project begins with a discovery call to define scope and fit. Once agreed, I send a fixed quote and a signed agreement. Payments are split — typically 50% before kickoff and 50% before launch, with larger projects broken into 40/30/30. No work starts until the first payment lands.',
  },
  {
    q: "What's included in the price, and what isn't?",
    a: "Each quote lists scope explicitly — what's included, what's out of scope, and what would be handled as an add-on. Third-party costs (domain, premium fonts, paid integrations) are always passed through transparently, never marked up.",
  },
  {
    q: "How do projects start, and what's the payment structure?",
    a: 'Every project begins with a discovery call to define scope and fit. Once agreed, I send a fixed quote and a signed agreement. Payments are split — typically 50% before kickoff and 50% before launch, with larger projects broken into 40/30/30. No work starts until the first payment lands.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Do you use AI in your work?',
    a: "AI is part of my workflow for research, drafting, and accelerating routine tasks. Every decision — design direction, code, structure, strategy — is reviewed and owned by me. AI assists. It doesn't deliver.",
  },
  {
    q: 'Can you work within an existing brand identity?',
    a: "Yes. If you have a brand book, design system, or established visual language, the site is built within it. If you don't, brand-level decisions become part of the project scope.",
  },
  {
    q: 'Who owns the files, design, and source code after launch?',
    a: 'You do. Full ownership of design files, Webflow project, and any associated assets transfers to you on final payment. Nothing is held hostage, ever.',
  },
  {
    q: 'What happens if I want to change something after launch?',
    a: "The site is built to be edited by non-technical users — most updates you'll handle yourself in Webflow's editor. Larger changes can be scoped separately. The first 14 days post-launch include support for anything that comes up.",
  },
  {
    q: 'How can I track progress during the project?',
    a: 'Once the project starts, you get access to a dedicated ClickUp workspace — tasks, calendar, Kanban board, files, and stage-by-stage progress. You see exactly what\'s happening in real time, without needing to ask.',
  },
];

